==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|cry over spilled milk}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-uk-dont cry over spilt milk.ogg|Audio (UK)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|cries over spilt milk|crying over spilt milk|cried over spilt milk}}

# To [[worry]] about [[unfortunate]] [[event]]s which have [[already]] [[happen]]ed and which cannot be [[change]]d.
#* {{quote-book|en|title=A Complete Collection of Genteel and Ingenious Conversation|author=Jonathan Swift|year=1738|passage='Tis a Folly to cry for spilt Milk.|authorlink=Jonathan Swift}}
#*{{quote-journal
|journal=The Sportsman's Cabinet, and Town and Country Magazine
|volume=1-2
|year=1833
|author=Mr. Warburton
|1=en
|page=376
|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=H9MKAQAAIAAJ&pg=RA15-PA6
|passage=The Willington Mare, when she started so fast, Ah! we little thought then that the race was her last: Accurst be the stake that was stained with her blood! But, why '''cry for spilt milk'''?—May the next be as good.}}
#*{{quote-book
|year=2016
|author=[[w:Barbara Hannay|Barbara Hannay]]
|title=The Grazier's Wife
|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=gFOMDAAAQBAJ&pg=PT9
|isbn=9781760142148
|publisher=Penguin Group Australia
|1=en
|passage=Don't you bloody dare '''cry over spilt milk'''. You only have yourself to blame.}}

====Usage notes====
* Usually found as a negative imperative: {{m|en||don't cry over spilt milk}} or {{m|en||there's no use crying over spilt milk}}.

